1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,420
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:07,549
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:10,719
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,804
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:19,144
[staff] <i>The girl who was with you, Ibyang.</i>

7
00:00:19,227 --> 00:00:21,229
She's in the lobby drinking water.

8
00:00:21,312 --> 00:00:22,939
She said she got lost
in the forest earlier.

9
00:00:23,022 --> 00:00:25,859
- [Atoy] <i>What about Janine?</i>
- [Gemma] <i>Oh, no! Why did they go there?</i>

10
00:00:25,942 --> 00:00:27,610
<i>There are monitor lizards</i>
<i>and snakes there.</i>

11
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:28,987
<i>Especially now, it's summer.</i>

12
00:00:29,070 --> 00:00:30,822
- [Atoy] <i>She was bitten by a snake.</i>
- [Audrey, in English] <i>Oh, no!</i>

13
00:00:30,905 --> 00:00:33,700
[Karla] <i>Where did you get this?</i>
<i>You never got those before.</i>

14
00:00:33,783 --> 00:00:34,701
<i>Is it Dad?</i>

15
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:37,996
This wouldn't have happened
to our daughter if Ibyang wasn't here!

16
00:00:38,079 --> 00:00:39,873
I know Ibyang.

17
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:41,249
She's not a bad child.

18
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:42,584
She wouldn't do that.

19
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,753
She deliberately made me get lost.

20
00:00:45,336 --> 00:00:47,046
Was that really her intention?

21
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:48,965
Don't you believe me?

22
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:51,009
- [woman] There are no women's clothes.
- [Karla] Ten pesos, one garment!

23
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,761
This is mine! These are my clothes, huh!

24
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:56,056
Everything I earn here,
I'll give to you so you can leave!

25
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:57,474
[sobs]

26
00:00:57,557 --> 00:01:00,602
[Cita] <i>I'll kill you first</i>
<i>before you kill my child.</i>

27
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:02,687
<i>We're done.</i>

28
00:01:02,771 --> 00:01:04,064
<i>Leave!</i>

29
00:01:04,147 --> 00:01:05,315
[Noel] You should be thankful

30
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:11,321
I accepted your child,
even if she's not mine!

31
00:01:11,404 --> 00:01:12,238
[Noel] <i>Delfin!</i>

32
00:01:13,114 --> 00:01:14,616
<i>Delfin is your father!</i>

33
00:01:14,699 --> 00:01:15,950
Atoy is your brother!

34
00:01:16,034 --> 00:01:17,202
[Audrey] <i>Your child is looking for you!</i>

35
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:18,703
She's not even your child!

36
00:01:18,787 --> 00:01:20,789
[Ibyang] <i>It's true.</i>

37
00:01:20,872 --> 00:01:23,083
[Audrey] <i>But you can only have one child.</i>

38
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:26,336
<i>Janine or Ibyang.</i>

39
00:01:26,419 --> 00:01:30,507
You fought with Aunt Audrey because of me.

40
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,342
Well, I believe you.

41
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:35,220
[Atoy] <i>I know</i>
<i>you didn't do anything wrong.</i>

42
00:01:35,303 --> 00:01:36,513
PREVIOUSLY

43
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:38,598
<i>Come on. I'll take you home.</i>

44
00:01:38,681 --> 00:01:40,850
[music fades]

45
00:01:42,393 --> 00:01:43,436
Sir Noel.

46
00:01:45,146 --> 00:01:46,606
You're really something else, huh?

47
00:01:47,482 --> 00:01:49,400
You know, ever since

48
00:01:49,484 --> 00:01:51,027
you lost your job,

49
00:01:52,028 --> 00:01:55,573
you've done nothing but cause trouble
here in our barangay, huh?

50
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,410
How can I help you?

51
00:02:00,036 --> 00:02:00,995
[scoffs]

52
00:02:01,079 --> 00:02:02,664
I don't need your help.

53
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:05,125
[scoffs]

54
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:07,252
Then who will help you?

55
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:09,671
Miss Cita?

56
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:11,756
[pensive music playing]

57
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,299
She already kicked you out, right?

58
00:02:13,383 --> 00:02:15,927
We'll reconcile!

59
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:18,138
We've been like this for a long time.

60
00:02:18,221 --> 00:02:19,264
We fight, then make up.

61
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:23,226
But in the end, I'm still her husband.

62
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:24,686
She can't do anything.

63
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:27,480
There's no divorce
here in the Philippines,

64
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:29,107
so she has no choice!

65
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:30,233
It's still me.

66
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:32,193
[sarcastic laugh] Okay.

67
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:34,821
So, you think…

68
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:39,576
You think Miss Cita won't leave you?

69
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:44,080
You almost stabbed her child
in front of her.

70
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:45,665
Right?

71
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:50,336
You should be taken
straight to the precinct. Huh?

72
00:02:51,588 --> 00:02:53,548
There's no divorce there,
but there is jail.

73
00:02:54,424 --> 00:02:55,508
[chuckles sarcastically]

74
00:02:56,009 --> 00:02:58,511
Hey, Paldo!

75
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:01,848
You act as if you have done no wrong.

76
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:04,475
Weren't you once the troublemaker
here in the barangay!

77
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:10,773
You even stole the statue of San Antonio--

78
00:03:10,857 --> 00:03:11,816
What?

79
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,526
[dramatic stinging]

80
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:15,445
That wasn't proven.

81
00:03:18,656 --> 00:03:20,658
If I was a troublemaker then…

82
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,244
I've changed.

83
00:03:24,495 --> 00:03:27,790
That's called character development.

84
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:32,712
Which you don't have,
because you never changed.

85
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:38,676
[Noel] Oh, see. She even came here.

86
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,719
She's here to pick me up.

87
00:03:39,802 --> 00:03:41,721
She'll coax me to come home--

88
00:03:41,804 --> 00:03:43,181
You got some nerve!

89
00:03:43,264 --> 00:03:45,642
You think I'm here to pick you up
to come home?!

90
00:03:45,725 --> 00:03:47,227
Here are your things!

91
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,896
Don't ever show yourself
to me and Karla again, huh!

92
00:03:50,730 --> 00:03:53,149
I'll press charges against you
for what you did to my child!

93
00:03:53,233 --> 00:03:54,692
Rot in jail!

94
00:03:54,776 --> 00:03:57,278
- Rot in jail!
- Cita. Cita!

95
00:03:57,362 --> 00:03:59,072
The nerve of you!

96
00:03:59,155 --> 00:04:00,573
Cita!

97
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:02,617
[tense music playing]

98
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,868
[Noel gasps]

99
00:04:05,995 --> 00:04:08,081
[music fades]

100
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:12,043
[suave theme music playing]

101
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:38,945
[music fades]

102
00:04:39,028 --> 00:04:40,196
[crickets chirping]

103
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,698
[Atoy] Oh, you should rest, Janine.

104
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:43,950
So we can do activities tomorrow.

105
00:04:44,951 --> 00:04:46,786
Uh, Daddy.

106
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,872
Can you sleep in my and Mommy's room,

107
00:04:49,956 --> 00:04:52,333
so we'll be complete, the three of us?

108
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:58,673
Uh, I'll let Ibyang know. All right.

109
00:04:59,799 --> 00:05:01,009
Go on, go inside.

110
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:04,721
My dear, you go ahead.

111
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:19,319
Have you talked to Ibyang?

112
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:22,071
[somber music playing]

113
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,531
Not yet.

114
00:05:24,240 --> 00:05:26,784
When do you plan to talk to her?

115
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:33,291
[melancholic music playing]

116
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:34,584
You know, Atoy…

117
00:05:36,127 --> 00:05:38,296
Let's not waste time.

118
00:05:40,339 --> 00:05:42,800
If you can't let go of Ibyang,

119
00:05:44,093 --> 00:05:45,636
I won't force you.

120
00:05:49,265 --> 00:05:51,392
But we can't be together

121
00:05:52,518 --> 00:05:55,188
if you can't choose our daughter.

122
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:56,773
Audrey.

123
00:05:58,066 --> 00:06:03,279
Maybe we made a mistake
trying to build this family.

124
00:06:04,155 --> 00:06:06,574
Stay here with Ibyang.

125
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:11,079
My child and I will go home.

126
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:12,997
Audrey, no. Don't.

127
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:14,791
[music fades]

128
00:06:14,874 --> 00:06:16,000
Don't leave.

129
00:06:18,586 --> 00:06:20,671
Okay? I love you and Janine.

130
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:25,218
[somber music playing]

131
00:06:25,301 --> 00:06:26,219
I want us to be whole.

132
00:06:26,302 --> 00:06:30,181
[sentimental music playing]

133
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:39,774
Karla is really unlucky
to have him as her dad.

134
00:06:39,857 --> 00:06:41,442
I mean, she's not even adopted,

135
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:44,028
and he has such
a bad attitude towards her.

136
00:06:44,112 --> 00:06:46,364
You know, you're the opposite.

137
00:06:46,447 --> 00:06:49,200
Because you, even if
you're not his real child,

138
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:51,119
Atoy loves you so much.

139
00:06:51,202 --> 00:06:52,829
Yes, that's true.

140
00:06:52,912 --> 00:06:53,913
[Ame] <i>Oh?</i>

141
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:56,582
Why does your voice sound sad?

142
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,836
Janine is the culprit again, isn't she?

143
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,754
What's the problem?

144
00:07:02,338 --> 00:07:06,300
I thought things
were okay with Aunt Audrey.

145
00:07:07,635 --> 00:07:13,766
But she made Tatoy choose
between me or Janine.

146
00:07:15,351 --> 00:07:16,436
Choose one, she said.

147
00:07:16,519 --> 00:07:17,353
Really?

148
00:07:18,062 --> 00:07:19,730
So, what did Atoy say?

149
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:21,357
I didn't hear, actually.

150
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:26,195
[melancholic music playing]

151
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:29,407
Ibyang, don't be sad, okay?

152
00:07:30,158 --> 00:07:33,202
I'm sure Atoy won't leave you.

153
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:35,872
[Ame] <i>He'll make a compromise.</i>

154
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:38,499
<i>And he won't just abandon you.</i>

155
00:07:39,083 --> 00:07:41,294
See, you're still there up to now.

156
00:07:41,377 --> 00:07:43,045
You're still together.

157
00:07:43,921 --> 00:07:44,964
That's true.

158
00:07:46,174 --> 00:07:47,633
All right then, Ibyang.

159
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:51,220
Go to sleep. It's late. Good night!

160
00:07:51,304 --> 00:07:52,555
Good night.

161
00:07:52,638 --> 00:07:58,769
[melodramatic music playing]

162
00:08:13,576 --> 00:08:15,953
[crickets chirping]

163
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:18,414
[phone vibrating]

164
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:23,419
Atoy.

165
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:29,509
What? Did Miss Cita call you?

166
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,678
She had a fight with Sir Noel.

167
00:08:33,179 --> 00:08:34,597
We brought him to the barangay.

168
00:08:35,097 --> 00:08:37,725
Anyway, I'll tell you the story later.

169
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:41,103
So, how was your vacation with the kids?

170
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:45,775
[pensive music playing]

171
00:08:46,484 --> 00:08:47,318
Huh?

172
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:49,987
Why are you asking me to fetch her?

173
00:08:50,821 --> 00:08:52,990
What's the problem
between Janine and Ibyang?

174
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:57,870
[heavy music playing]

175
00:09:06,754 --> 00:09:08,798
'Son, thank you.

176
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,175
Have you told Ibyang yet?

177
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:13,553
[Atoy] Not yet.

178
00:09:15,179 --> 00:09:16,097
Wait--

179
00:09:16,847 --> 00:09:17,723
[Ibyang] Oh?

180
00:09:17,807 --> 00:09:19,350
Brother Emerson!

181
00:09:19,433 --> 00:09:20,601
You're here too?

182
00:09:21,435 --> 00:09:23,729
Are you joining us for fishing?

183
00:09:25,439 --> 00:09:27,733
Uh, Ibyang. Come here for a moment.

184
00:09:27,817 --> 00:09:30,528
Um, I just need
to tell you something, okay?

185
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:32,488
[clears throat]

186
00:09:34,073 --> 00:09:37,118
Your Brother Emerson is here…

187
00:09:38,619 --> 00:09:41,789
to take you home, to accompany you.

188
00:09:41,872 --> 00:09:43,583
[somber music playing]

189
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,008
I'm sorry, Ibyang.

190
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,343
[melancholic music playing]

191
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:57,722
This is hard for me too, but…

192
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:05,730
this is so you and Janine
won't fight anymore, okay?

193
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:12,320
But I thought you believed me?

194
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:14,614
Yes, I believe you.

195
00:10:15,865 --> 00:10:19,160
And I'm proud of you
because you still do the right thing,

196
00:10:19,243 --> 00:10:21,203
even when no one is watching.

197
00:10:21,287 --> 00:10:22,997
That's what I always tell you.

198
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:26,292
[dramatic flourish]

199
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,966
[melodramatic music playing]

200
00:10:36,844 --> 00:10:40,556
But why are you sending me home?

201
00:10:42,892 --> 00:10:45,436
I didn't do anything wrong.

202
00:10:46,979 --> 00:10:49,607
Why are you punishing me?

203
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:52,943
No, no.

204
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:54,654
I'm not punishing you.

205
00:10:55,946 --> 00:10:58,991
I'm not. I'm not punishing you.

206
00:10:59,075 --> 00:11:00,451
I'm just saying…

207
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:08,542
I'm only doing this for Janine, okay?

208
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:11,462
I hope you understand, Ibyang.

209
00:11:14,298 --> 00:11:16,801
So, you chose Janine?

210
00:11:19,762 --> 00:11:22,098
You won't adopt me anymore?

211
00:11:22,765 --> 00:11:25,935
[dramatic music playing]

212
00:11:39,156 --> 00:11:40,282
Lord…

213
00:11:41,409 --> 00:11:43,452
Lord, am I a bad person if…

214
00:11:44,328 --> 00:11:46,747
I chose my own child over Ibyang?

215
00:11:46,831 --> 00:11:49,500
[music fades]

216
00:11:52,128 --> 00:11:53,379
[in English] I'm sorry.

217
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:56,924
Mommy?

218
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:58,968
You're crying?

219
00:11:59,802 --> 00:12:00,803
Why?

220
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:06,100
Your daddy is sending Ibyang home.

221
00:12:06,183 --> 00:12:07,852
[heavy music playing]

222
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,645
I'm crying because…

223
00:12:12,314 --> 00:12:14,275
I just feel sorry for her.

224
00:12:15,401 --> 00:12:18,404
But this is the only way I know…

225
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:20,448
so there won't be any more conflict.

226
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:23,701
Mommy, don't cry anymore,

227
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:25,244
because you and Daddy are back together,

228
00:12:25,327 --> 00:12:26,787
and we're complete now.

229
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:32,168
We want you to feel that Daddy
and I love you very much, child.

230
00:12:41,510 --> 00:12:42,928
[sighs, then sobs]

231
00:12:43,012 --> 00:12:44,889
[music fades]

232
00:12:44,972 --> 00:12:47,683
[intense music playing]

233
00:12:51,103 --> 00:12:52,646
[sobbing]

234
00:12:54,106 --> 00:12:56,442
[wailing]

235
00:12:56,525 --> 00:12:57,485
[melancholic music playing]

236
00:12:57,568 --> 00:13:00,196
[wailing]

237
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,246
This isn't easy for me either, Ibyang.

238
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,457
[sobbing]

239
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:12,666
That's enough.

240
00:13:12,750 --> 00:13:13,834
I'm sorry.

241
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:17,880
[sobbing]

242
00:13:23,511 --> 00:13:28,015
I'll never have a real family.

243
00:13:28,098 --> 00:13:30,518
No. You'll still have a real family.

244
00:13:32,353 --> 00:13:35,314
Huh? I'm still here.

245
00:13:36,357 --> 00:13:37,691
You have Miss Cita.

246
00:13:38,359 --> 00:13:39,818
And you have Sister Karla.

247
00:13:39,902 --> 00:13:42,029
You can still come
to the house anytime you want.

248
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:44,573
[Atoy] But of course,

249
00:13:45,991 --> 00:13:48,994
it's different
when you have a real family,

250
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:51,830
when you're the top priority.

251
00:13:52,706 --> 00:13:57,419
A father and mother
who think of no one else but you,

252
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:59,672
and that’s what I’ll look for, for you.

253
00:14:00,798 --> 00:14:01,882
[sobs]

254
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:05,052
But you're the father I want.

255
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:08,472
You're the best!

256
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:10,975
[sobbing]

257
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:19,400
I'm sure there's someone else
out there who's even better.

258
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:24,363
But he won't be Tatoy.

259
00:14:24,446 --> 00:14:25,906
[sobbing]

260
00:14:31,412 --> 00:14:32,580
Come on. Ibyang, let's go.

261
00:14:33,497 --> 00:14:35,708
- No, I don't want to!
- Come on.

262
00:14:35,791 --> 00:14:37,585
- [melodramatic music playing]
- [indistinct]

263
00:14:37,668 --> 00:14:40,045
[Ibyang] I don't want to.

264
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,757
Come on. All right. You should go now.

265
00:14:43,841 --> 00:14:45,050
Do you want a treat?

266
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:48,012
What do you want, huh?

267
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:49,388
When I come back.

268
00:14:49,471 --> 00:14:50,890
Do you want siomai?

269
00:14:51,473 --> 00:14:53,350
Pares? Do you want pares?

270
00:14:54,059 --> 00:14:55,519
Come on.

271
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:56,896
[Emerson] Come on, come on.

272
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:58,772
Go, go on.

273
00:14:58,856 --> 00:14:59,940
Come on, come on.

274
00:15:00,024 --> 00:15:01,442
I just wish…

275
00:15:02,902 --> 00:15:05,946
I was your real child.

276
00:15:07,948 --> 00:15:10,618
So you wouldn't give me away.

277
00:15:12,786 --> 00:15:15,497
You're my only Tatoy.

278
00:15:18,834 --> 00:15:20,085
And you're my only Ibyang.

279
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:23,339
- [dramatic music playing]
- [Atoy] Go on.

280
00:15:26,216 --> 00:15:27,676
[sobbing]

281
00:16:03,504 --> 00:16:05,255
[Ame] Why is Atoy like that?

282
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:08,425
Choosing that troublesome Janine?

283
00:16:11,053 --> 00:16:13,722
[Emerson] Ame, that's his child.

284
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:15,265
Of course, he'll choose her.

285
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:18,185
But he should have fought for Ibyang.

286
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:20,354
[melancholic music playing]

287
00:16:20,437 --> 00:16:23,107
Believe me, it's hard for him too.

288
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:25,067
He couldn't even say it.

289
00:16:25,150 --> 00:16:27,027
Don't make him out to be the villain.

290
00:16:28,153 --> 00:16:29,947
[Ame] He gave the child false hope.

291
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:31,573
He promised her.

292
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:34,034
That's really painful for Ibyang.

293
00:16:34,618 --> 00:16:37,329
Look at her!
She's never cried like this before!

294
00:16:37,413 --> 00:16:39,248
[Emerson clicks tongue] Yes.

295
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:42,418
I can feel her pain.

296
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:46,797
So, imagine how Atoy must feel.

297
00:16:47,965 --> 00:16:50,009
But Atoy has a family.

298
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,053
He shouldn't have promised to adopt Ibyang

299
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,264
if he wasn't going to do it.

300
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:03,439
[sobbing]

301
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,110
[Ame] Ibyang…

302
00:17:08,861 --> 00:17:10,738
I'm here, okay?

303
00:17:12,239 --> 00:17:13,532
Sister Ame…

304
00:17:16,493 --> 00:17:20,873
I'm used to it being just the two of us.

305
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,750
[melodramatic music playing]

306
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:25,544
[sobbing] If Tatoy doesn't want me,

307
00:17:26,503 --> 00:17:27,838
then fine.

308
00:17:31,967 --> 00:17:35,679
I won't force myself…

309
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,892
on someone who can't choose me.

310
00:17:42,352 --> 00:17:44,271
That's enough.

311
00:17:44,354 --> 00:17:46,523
Sis Ame is here, okay?

312
00:17:46,607 --> 00:17:47,691
[hushing]

313
00:17:47,775 --> 00:17:48,776
Come here.

314
00:17:48,859 --> 00:17:51,779
- [wailing]
- [dramatic music playing]

315
00:17:52,946 --> 00:17:54,865
I'm here.

316
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:12,091
FATHER'S LANE
FOOD HUB IN BACLARAN

317
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:13,801
[woman] Sis, let's go. Come on!

318
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:15,803
I don't want to. I don't have--
I don't have money.

319
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:19,181
- Miss Cita, are you okay?
- Yes.

320
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:21,266
Psst. Hey, Cita.

321
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:23,227
Did Noel get out of jail?

322
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:25,562
What? Did he fight with you again?

323
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:26,772
Huh?

324
00:18:26,855 --> 00:18:27,856
No.

325
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,274
I'm looking for my daughter.

326
00:18:29,358 --> 00:18:31,985
- Have you seen Karla?
- Karla?

327
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:32,986
- Seems like--
- No, no.

328
00:18:33,070 --> 00:18:34,655
Well, maybe your daughter
is still sleeping.

329
00:18:34,738 --> 00:18:35,989
It's still early.

330
00:18:36,073 --> 00:18:38,492
- I checked her room. She wasn't there.
- [woman] Hmm?

331
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:40,160
She wasn't at the basketball court either.

332
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:42,204
Where could she have gone?

333
00:18:42,704 --> 00:18:44,456
- Oh, I saw her!
- [woman] Oh, oh!

334
00:18:44,540 --> 00:18:45,457
Where?

335
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:46,625
She rode a jeepney.

336
00:18:46,708 --> 00:18:48,335
Looked like it was bound for San Roque.

337
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:49,586
- A jeepney?
- Yes, she got on a jeep.

338
00:18:49,670 --> 00:18:50,921
[both] What?

339
00:18:51,004 --> 00:18:54,424
[suspicious music playing]

340
00:18:59,096 --> 00:19:02,724
[music fades]

341
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:08,897
[birds chirping]

342
00:19:10,774 --> 00:19:11,608
Dad…

343
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:17,364
It must feel good
to say that face-to-face, right?

344
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,286
For the longest time,

345
00:19:23,078 --> 00:19:25,122
I really thought of you as my father.

346
00:19:25,664 --> 00:19:26,915
[sentimental music playing]

347
00:19:26,999 --> 00:19:28,542
But now that I learned it's true,

348
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:31,044
I don't know how I should feel.

349
00:19:33,255 --> 00:19:34,756
I'm happy,

350
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:36,842
but…

351
00:19:38,594 --> 00:19:40,262
it's embarrassing.

352
00:19:41,638 --> 00:19:44,474
I'm the result of your betrayal of Mom.

353
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:53,483
I don't even know if you knew
I was your child.

354
00:20:00,490 --> 00:20:02,868
Delfin knew you were his youngest.

355
00:20:03,493 --> 00:20:06,747
[melodramatic music playing]

356
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,884
[wind chimes clinking]

357
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:20,969
[music fades]

358
00:20:21,053 --> 00:20:22,137
Ibyang!

359
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:26,016
Miss Cita?

360
00:20:27,768 --> 00:20:28,936
[sighs]

361
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:31,063
Ibyang?

362
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:36,818
'Nang?

363
00:20:38,737 --> 00:20:39,613
[knocks on door]

364
00:20:39,696 --> 00:20:41,114
- 'Toy.
- Oh?

365
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,658
- Mmm, bro.
- Oh?

366
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:44,660
What's this? Is this your gift for us?

367
00:20:44,743 --> 00:20:45,577
Psst, hey.

368
00:20:45,661 --> 00:20:47,579
Don't touch that. It's Ibyang's.

369
00:20:48,455 --> 00:20:49,665
[Atoy] Where are they?

370
00:20:52,709 --> 00:20:53,710
I don't know.

371
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:56,171
Hmm, I just left them here last night.

372
00:20:56,255 --> 00:21:00,342
[mysterious music playing]

373
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:06,974
ATOY, IBYANG AND I LEFT
THE CHILD WANTED TO DO SO

374
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,850
DON'T COME AND FIND US

375
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:12,562
They left?

376
00:21:15,023 --> 00:21:16,566
Why didn't you tell me?

377
00:21:17,859 --> 00:21:19,736
I didn't know, 'Toy.

378
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:23,740
Last night, I just left them here.
They were sad.

379
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:27,202
I didn't hear anything about leaving.

380
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:29,621
Where could they have gone?

381
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:33,625
[music fades]

382
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:36,003
Forgive me.

383
00:21:37,087 --> 00:21:39,006
I didn't tell you the truth.

384
00:21:40,674 --> 00:21:43,468
I planned to take
this secret to the grave,

385
00:21:44,428 --> 00:21:46,221
just like Delfin did.

386
00:21:49,808 --> 00:21:52,728
Why didn't Dad tell me?

387
00:21:52,811 --> 00:21:55,022
[melancholic music playing]

388
00:21:55,105 --> 00:21:57,482
We agreed not to tell you.

389
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,487
He forgave me, but…

390
00:22:03,697 --> 00:22:05,198
he didn't forgive Delfin.

391
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:10,620
That's why he poured all his anger on you.

392
00:22:20,172 --> 00:22:23,300
That's why I never felt that Dad loved me.

393
00:22:27,054 --> 00:22:29,890
That's why he was always angry with me.

394
00:22:29,973 --> 00:22:32,225
[melodramatic music playing]

395
00:22:32,309 --> 00:22:34,728
Because I'm the outcome of your sin.

396
00:22:35,353 --> 00:22:36,855
Forgive me.

397
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:41,693
[sobs] I didn't defend you
against Noel before.

398
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:47,616
I absorbed and accepted
all his hurtful words.

399
00:22:47,699 --> 00:22:49,993
Because it was my fault,

400
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:51,703
so I had to accept it.

401
00:22:55,373 --> 00:22:56,792
But what about Brother Atoy?

402
00:22:57,793 --> 00:23:00,045
Did he just accept everything too?

403
00:23:00,128 --> 00:23:02,172
[music fades]

404
00:23:02,255 --> 00:23:03,548
He doesn't know.

405
00:23:04,925 --> 00:23:06,218
What?!

406
00:23:06,301 --> 00:23:08,053
[heavy music playing]

407
00:23:08,136 --> 00:23:11,515
So, he looks like an idiot too,
because he doesn't know the truth?

408
00:23:13,725 --> 00:23:15,894
Mom, we should tell him.

409
00:23:15,977 --> 00:23:19,272
Do you think I don't want to tell him?

410
00:23:20,482 --> 00:23:24,152
[sobs] Do you think I don't
want to ask his forgiveness?

411
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:29,741
I regret all my sins, Karla.

412
00:23:29,825 --> 00:23:31,701
Believe me.

413
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:37,332
But Delfin made me promise
not to tell Atoy,

414
00:23:37,415 --> 00:23:41,586
because he didn't want his son
to have no one to trust.

415
00:23:41,670 --> 00:23:43,463
So, what now?

416
00:23:44,506 --> 00:23:47,342
You want me to join you in fooling us?

417
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:51,638
Pretend everything's fine?

418
00:23:52,973 --> 00:23:54,766
That everything's back to normal?

419
00:23:55,725 --> 00:23:56,726
[Cita] My child…

420
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:57,644
[sobs]

421
00:23:57,727 --> 00:24:00,647
Sorry, Mom, but I can't do that.

422
00:24:03,024 --> 00:24:07,320
Brother Atoy is so kind to us.
He deserves to know the truth.

423
00:24:07,404 --> 00:24:09,489
That's the problem!

424
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:13,285
Do you want to repay
his kindness with pain?

425
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:17,914
Karla, I'm begging you.

426
00:24:17,998 --> 00:24:22,335
If he finds out the truth,
surely, he won't forgive me.

427
00:24:22,919 --> 00:24:24,754
Promise me, Karla.

428
00:24:25,463 --> 00:24:28,550
[sobs] You won't tell him.

429
00:24:28,633 --> 00:24:32,179
[somber music playing]

430
00:24:36,474 --> 00:24:38,935
[sobbing]

431
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:42,147
[epic music playing]

432
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:49,613
[birds chirping]

433
00:24:50,197 --> 00:24:52,073
Full!

434
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:54,159
Thank you, Miss Cita.

435
00:24:55,076 --> 00:24:58,079
Um, I still have a little money.

436
00:24:58,163 --> 00:24:59,789
We'll contribute here.

437
00:24:59,873 --> 00:25:02,417
No, don't think about that.

438
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,169
This house is open for you,

439
00:25:04,252 --> 00:25:06,838
and it's even better
that you're staying here with me.

440
00:25:09,090 --> 00:25:11,134
And Sis Karla?

441
00:25:11,927 --> 00:25:13,470
Is she okay?

442
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:17,974
Because last night she seemed sad.

443
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:19,643
She didn't talk to me.

444
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:21,978
Does she have a problem?

445
00:25:22,729 --> 00:25:24,689
[Ame] What problem would Karla have?

446
00:25:25,523 --> 00:25:29,361
She should be happy now,
since Sir Noel is gone.

447
00:25:30,111 --> 00:25:31,446
- [Atoy] 'Nang?
- [Ame] Hey.

448
00:25:31,529 --> 00:25:32,572
- [Ame] Hey.
- [Atoy] 'Nang!

449
00:25:32,656 --> 00:25:34,574
- It's Atoy.
- [knocks on door]

450
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:36,284
- [Atoy] Godmother Cita!
- It's A--Iit's Atoy.

451
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:39,663
[suspicious music playing]

452
00:25:39,746 --> 00:25:40,747
[Cita] Um…

453
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:42,540
[Atoy] 'Nang!

454
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:47,128
How are you?

455
00:25:52,008 --> 00:25:55,720
Well, Ibyang left me.

456
00:25:57,681 --> 00:25:59,349
She's upset with me.

457
00:25:59,432 --> 00:26:00,475
She's sulking.

458
00:26:04,145 --> 00:26:08,024
[sneaky music playing]

459
00:26:10,652 --> 00:26:11,653
Godmother…

460
00:26:13,822 --> 00:26:15,240
Are they here?

461
00:26:16,074 --> 00:26:19,661
[tense music playing]

462
00:26:33,675 --> 00:26:34,884
Wow, you look different.

463
00:26:34,968 --> 00:26:37,721
You're sharper than a needle.

464
00:26:37,804 --> 00:26:38,763
Oh my God!

465
00:26:39,306 --> 00:26:41,141
Is it true, Atoy?

466
00:26:41,224 --> 00:26:42,726
That… you're like a secret killer spy?

467
00:26:42,809 --> 00:26:44,394
[Red] <i>You need to talk to Audrey.</i>

468
00:26:44,477 --> 00:26:47,230
Tell her it's a bad idea
to get back together with Atoy.

469
00:26:47,314 --> 00:26:48,398
What's wrong with that?

470
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:50,108
I hit-and-run Atoy's father.

471
00:26:50,191 --> 00:26:52,444
Our family will be destroyed
if those two end up together.

472
00:26:52,527 --> 00:26:54,321
UP NEXT

473
00:26:54,404 --> 00:26:56,364
You're not just a tracker,

474
00:26:56,448 --> 00:26:57,824
you're also a marksman.

475
00:26:57,907 --> 00:26:59,284
Just inspired, sir.

476
00:26:59,367 --> 00:27:01,995
And this is what I'll do
to the one who ran over my father.

477
00:27:04,331 --> 00:27:06,082
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

478
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:08,001
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

479
00:27:08,084 --> 00:27:11,546
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

480
00:27:11,629 --> 00:27:13,423
♪ <i>Fix it</i> ♪

481
00:27:13,506 --> 00:27:14,424
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
